# Forked Repository Evidence

This file is intended to hold proof — via the GitHub API — that this repository
is a fork of:

    ibm-developer-skills-network/mcino-Introduction-to-Git-and-GitHub

This evidence can only be produced from your own, real GitHub repository after
you have forked it. It cannot be fabricated here.

## EXPECTED COMMAND TO RUN

Run the following command in your terminal, replacing the placeholders with
your real GitHub username and your real repository name:

```bash
curl -L https://api.github.com/repos/YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME/YOUR_REPOSITORY_NAME
```

Replace:

- `YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME` — your actual GitHub username
- `YOUR_REPOSITORY_NAME` — the actual name of your forked repository

## WHAT TO VERIFY IN THE RESPONSE

In the JSON response returned by the command above, check the following field:

- `"fork"` — this should be `true`, confirming the repository is a fork
- `"parent"` — this object (in particular `parent.full_name`) should read
  `ibm-developer-skills-network/mcino-Introduction-to-Git-and-GitHub`,
  confirming the exact upstream repository this was forked from

These two fields together are the proof Coursera is asking you to capture.

